  "title": "Leise rieselt der Schnee",
  "composer": "Traditional",
  "about": "Leise rieselt der Schnee means Softly falls the snow in German. It is one of the best-known Advent songs in the German language. The pastor Eduard Ebel wrote the words in 1895, and his book printed them with no melody. Many books credit the tune to Ebel too, but no source shows it, and others call it a folk tune.",
  "funFact": "Some say the tune grew from a Musette by Daniel Gottlob Türk from 1792, but only its first bar and a half match.",
